shot    gnugo
size    24 80
cap     GNU Go on the full 19x19 board, a few moves in.  It asks the
cap     handicap and which colour you take, then plays: moves are a column
cap     letter and a row number -- A to T with I left out, 1 to 19 -- and
cap     `pass', `save' and `stop' do what they say.  It counts the score
cap     when both sides pass.
try     gnugo
run     clear
wait    1
run     gnugo
wait    3
send    \r
wait    2
send    0\r
wait    2
send    b\r
wait    3
send    D4\r
wait    6
snap
send    stop\rn\r
wait    3

shot    bjack
size    24 80
cap     A stake of $500 and a first bet of 100, dealt from one shuffled deck.
cap     The dealer's second card is the `?'; the game then asks each decision
cap     the hand allows -- double, hit, split, insurance -- in turn.
try     bjack 500
run     clear
wait    1
run     bjack 500
wait    3
send    100\r
wait    3

shot    hanoi
size    24 80
cap     The seven moves that shift three disks from tower 1 to tower 2,
cap     never setting a larger disk on a smaller one.
try     hanoi 3
run     clear
wait    1
run     hanoi 3
wait    2

shot    hanoimod
size    24 80
cap     The three-disk solution drawn as towers: after each move, a line per
cap     tower lists the disks on it, largest first.  The first five of seven
cap     moves.
try     hanoimod 3 | head -n 20
os9     hanoimod 3 ! head -n 20
run     clear
wait    1
run     hanoimod 3 | head -n 20
wait    2

shot    knight
size    24 80
